Le Wi-Fi se configure dans RÃ©glages. Les radios viennent de /radios.json, les albums de /Audio, les vidÃ©os de /Video ou /videos.json. Les vidÃ©os prises en charge sont AVI/MJPEG et MJPEG brut. Ã‰chap quitte la vidÃ©o en plein Ã©cran.

Le changement dâ€™application peut laisser lâ€™audio actif. Utilisez Pause ou ArrÃªter pour interrompre lâ€™Ã©coute. Les erreurs de dÃ©marrage et de lecture sont signalÃ©es. Aucun contrÃ´le mÃ©moire pÃ©riodique ne purge les applications ni nâ€™interrompt la radio. RÃ©glages â†’ SystÃ¨me permet de consulter les ressources disponibles.

La loupe ou Ctrl+F filtre lâ€™onglet actif : morceaux de tous les albums, stations de toutes les catÃ©gories radio, enregistrements ou vidÃ©os. Chaque onglet garde ses propres mots de recherche. La croix enlÃ¨ve le filtre ; choisir un rÃ©sultat lance lâ€™Ã©lÃ©ment correspondant. Les noms, dossiers et catÃ©gories peuvent Ãªtre recherchÃ©s sans tenir compte de la casse ou des accents latins.

Musique parcourt les sous-dossiers de /Audio et /mp3. + dans le panneau gauche crÃ©e une sous-catÃ©gorie. Pour les radios, une catÃ©gorie Jazz/Piano crÃ©e deux niveaux. Le + Ã  droite dâ€™un morceau ou dâ€™une radio ajoute un favori ; la coche le retire. Favoris filtre la liste de lâ€™onglet courant. Ils sont conservÃ©s sur la SD.␀␀␀␀Choose a radio category, album or recording, then an item to play. On a keyboard, Up/Down select and Enter plays. Space toggles play / pause; Alt+Left / Right selects the previous / next track. These keys retain their normal use in text fields.

Configure Wi-Fi in Settings. Stations come from /radios.json, albums from /Audio, and videos from /Video or /videos.json. Supported video formats are AVI/MJPEG and raw MJPEG. Escape leaves full-screen video.

Changing apps can leave audio playing. Use Pause or Stop to end playback. Startup and playback errors are reported. No periodic memory check clears applications or interrupts the radio. Settings -> System shows available resources.

The magnifying glass or Ctrl+F filters the active tab: tracks from all albums, stations from all radio categories, recordings or videos. Each tab keeps its own search words. The cross clears the filter; choosing a result plays the matching item. Names, folders and categories can be searched regardless of Latin case or accents.

Music browses subfolders of /Audio and /mp3. + in the left panel creates a subcategory. For radio, a category such as Jazz/Piano creates two levels. + on a track or station adds a favorite; the checkmark removes it. Favorites filters the current tab. Favorites are saved on the SD card.␀␀␀␀Choose a radio category, album or recording, then an item to play. On a keyboard, Up/Down select and Enter plays. Space toggles play / pause; Alt+Left / Right selects the previous / next track. These keys retain their normal use in text fields.

Configure Wi-Fi in Settings. Stations come from /radios.json, albums from /Audio, and videos from /Video or /videos.json. Supported video formats are AVI/MJPEG and raw MJPEG. Escape leaves full-screen video.

Changing apps can leave audio playing. Use Pause or Stop to end playback. Startup and playback errors are reported. No periodic memory check clears applications or interrupts the radio. Settings -> System shows available resources.

The magnifying glass or Ctrl+F filters the active tab: tracks from all albums, stations from all radio categories, recordings or videos. Each tab keeps its own search words. The cross clears the filter; choosing a result plays the matching item. Names, folders and categories can be searched regardless of Latin case or accents.

Music browses subfolders of /Audio and /mp3. The + on the left creates a subcategory. A radio category such as Jazz/Piano creates two levels. The star adds or removes a favourite. The Favourites selector filters the list; favourites remain saved on the SD card.

Volume, including zero, is retained after restarting. Media restores the tab, Favourites filter and last selection without starting playback.␀␀Cible␀␀␀Target␀␀Cible : ␀␀␀␀Target: ␀␀␀␀Cible MicroPython␀␀␀MicroPython target␀␀Cible dÃ©clarÃ©e â€” compatibilitÃ© non testÃ©e␀Declared target - compatibility untested␀␀␀␀Classic
