Les packs /System/languages/*.json dÃ©finissent la langue de l'interface, aide et messages compris. Le franÃ§ais utilise aussi son fichier SD lorsqu'il est prÃ©sent. Une traduction absente revient Ã  l'anglais, sauf pour le franÃ§ais qui conserve son libellÃ© source.

Si la police SD manque ou ne peut pas Ãªtre chargÃ©e, l'interface passe temporairement en anglais avec la police intÃ©grÃ©e. La langue choisie reste enregistrÃ©e. RedÃ©marrer avec une police disponible rÃ©tablit cette langue ; les documents ne sont jamais traduits ni modifiÃ©s. RedÃ©marrez aussi aprÃ¨s avoir changÃ© les packs de langue pour les recharger.

Le clavier peut suivre la langue de lâ€™interface ou Ãªtre choisi sÃ©parÃ©ment dans RÃ©glages â†’ Langue ; les quinze dispositions fournies sâ€™appliquent aux claviers tactile et USB. Le chinois utilise le pinyin, le japonais les romaji/kana avec choix de candidats et le corÃ©en la composition hangul ; Ctrl+Espace alterne avec la saisie latine.

Une police compatible doit contenir les caractÃ¨res de la langue. La date, lâ€™heure, le fuseau, NTP et le Wi-Fi se rÃ¨glent dans leurs rubriques. F1 reste disponible pour retrouver cette aide.

Sans clavier USB dÃ©tectÃ©, toucher un champ de saisie ouvre le clavier tactile. Avec un clavier USB, il reste fermÃ© automatiquement ; son bouton permet de lâ€™ouvrir volontairement. La flÃ¨che vers le bas ferme toujours le clavier ; EntrÃ©e le ferme aussi dans un champ sur une ligne.␀␀␀Enter opens the selected setting, arrows adjust its value and Escape returns to the controls. In Settings -> Interface -> Display, the Theme list applies immediately and Corner radius adjusts control shapes; brightness and text size remain independent.

Packs in /System/languages/*.json define the interface language, including help and messages. French also uses its SD pack when present. Missing translations fall back to English, except French retains the source label.

If the SD font is missing or cannot load, the interface temporarily switches to English with the built-in font. The selected language remains saved. Restarting with an available font restores that language; documents are never translated or changed. Also restart after editing language packs to reload them.

The keyboard can follow the interface language or be chosen separately in Settings -> Language; the fifteen supplied layouts apply to both touch and USB keyboards. Chinese uses pinyin, Japanese uses romaji/kana with candidate selection, and Korean uses Hangul composition; Ctrl+Space switches to and from Latin input.

A compatible font must contain the language's characters. Date, time, time zone, NTP and Wi-Fi have their own settings. F1 remains available to return to this help.

Without a detected USB keyboard, touching an input opens the on-screen keyboard. With a USB keyboard, it stays closed automatically; its button can open it manually. The down arrow always closes it; Enter also closes it in a single-line field.␀␀␀␀Enter opens the selected setting, arrows adjust its value and Escape returns to the controls. In Settings -> Interface -> Display, the Theme list applies immediately and Corner radius adjusts control shapes; brightness and text size remain independent.

Packs in /System/languages/*.json define the interface language, including help and messages. French also uses its SD pack when present. Missing translations fall back to English, except French retains the source label.

If the SD font is missing or cannot load, the interface temporarily switches to English with the built-in font. The selected language remains saved. Restarting with an available font restores that language; documents are never translated or changed. Also restart after editing language packs to reload them.

Choose the keyboard separately in Settings -> Language. The fifteen layouts apply to touch and USB keyboards. Chinese uses pinyin, Japanese romaji/kana and Korean Hangul composition; Ctrl+Space switches to and from Latin input.

A compatible font must contain the language's characters. Date, time, time zone, NTP and Wi-Fi have their own settings. F1 remains available to return to this help.

