Escape: quit - F1: hide help␀Function requires parentheses␀␀␀Unknown function␀␀␀␀Background␀␀Fond du texte␀␀␀Text background␀Fonts␀␀␀Strength␀␀␀␀Format␀␀Format attendu : AAAA-MM-JJ HH:MM␀␀␀Expected format: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM␀␀␀Unreadable audio format␀Format audio incompatible␀␀␀Unsupported audio format␀␀␀␀Format de carte non pris en charge␀␀Unsupported map format␀␀Format de papier non pris en charge␀Paper size not supported␀␀␀␀Invalid device vault format␀Invalid vault format␀␀␀␀Format dâ€™illustration non pris en charge␀␀Unsupported illustration format␀Format dâ€™image non pris en charge␀Unsupported image format␀␀␀␀Format and resolution␀␀␀Format image non pris en charge␀Format non pris en charge par le lecteur web␀␀␀␀Format unsupported by the web reader␀␀␀␀Format -> Color settings (Ctrl+Shift+C) chooses text and background colors separately. Choosing a swatch does not change the document. Text color (Ctrl+Alt+C) and Text background (Ctrl+Alt+H) affect the selection, or subsequent typing if nothing is selected. Table cells support these styles too. Escape closes the palette. The keyboard button is directly on the Editor toolbar and in the table editor. L+ and C+ immediately show the new row or column; Apply saves the table into the document.

JPG now captures the map already displayed at its current resolution, without increasing zoom or downloading more tiles. Wait until the desired details are visible before capturing. Credits remain below the image. The file is created in /Picture/Maps/map-NNNN.jpg.

A small panel keeps progress visible during copying and encoding. The cross or Escape cancels; changing the view during copying also cancels that stage. JPEG encoding runs by scanlines. No incomplete file is published. Writing -> Insert -> Image inserts the result.

