Dans Explorateur, le cadenas chiffre ou dÃ©chiffre une copie du fichier. Les originaux et les sauvegardes ordinaires de l'Ã©diteur restent lisibles. Le coffre protÃ¨ge les fichiers choisis sur une carte retirÃ©e ; sa fermeture ne protÃ¨ge pas tous les documents ni la mÃ©moire interne de l'appareil.␀The device vault opens natively on this Tab5, with no password or code to copy. On first use, choose Create device vault. Close or turning off the screen clears the in-memory session; opening it again retrieves the local keys without entry. Anyone using this Tab5 can therefore open this vault: it does not lock the device.

The legacy vault is preserved. Its original password is still required to recover its keys, and opening it may take time. In Vault access, Open legacy vault followed by Copy keys to device vault migrates the keys without deleting the original keyring. Creating a new device vault does not decrypt older files when their key is missing.

Manage keys lets you back up each key in a password-protected .t5key file and restore it. Keep these backups on another medium together with their passwords. An SD card alone is not enough after losing or erasing the Tab5: without a key or usable backup, encrypted files are lost.

In Files, the padlock encrypts or decrypts a copy. Originals and ordinary editor backups remain readable. The vault protects selected files on a removed card; closing it does not protect every document or the device's internal memory.␀␀Le coffre appareil s'ouvre nativement sur ce Tab5. Dans AccÃ¨s du coffre, un PIN facultatif de 4 Ã  12 chiffres limite l'ouverture ; il peut Ãªtre modifiÃ© ou retirÃ© aprÃ¨s dÃ©verrouillage. Verrouiller ou Ã©teindre l'Ã©cran ferme la session. Sans PIN, toute personne utilisant ce Tab5 peut ouvrir le coffre.

