Coffre de mots de passe enregistre jusqu'Ã  64 identifiants, tokens ou mots de passe sous un nom de variable. Nouveau, Enregistrer et Supprimer gÃ¨rent les entrÃ©es. Afficher / masquer change la visibilitÃ© du champ ; Copier garde la valeur 30 secondes dans le presse-papiers. Le terminal, MicroPython et les applications peuvent lire ces valeurs tant que le coffre est dÃ©verrouillÃ©. Git peut rÃ©fÃ©rencer deux entrÃ©es pour l'identifiant et le jeton. Un programme peut conserver ou divulguer une valeur dÃ©jÃ  reÃ§ue, mÃªme aprÃ¨s verrouillage ; utilisez des programmes de confiance.␀␀␀The device vault opens natively on this Tab5. In Vault access, an optional 4 to 12 digit PIN restricts opening; it can be changed or removed after unlocking. Lock or turning off the screen closes the session. Without a PIN, anyone using this Tab5 can open the vault.

The legacy vault is preserved. Its original password is still required to recover its keys, and opening it may take time. In Vault access, Open legacy vault followed by Copy keys to device vault migrates the keys without deleting the original keyring. Creating a new device vault does not decrypt older files when their key is missing.

Keys, including the initial key, can be deleted after confirmation. Without a backup of a key, its encrypted files become unrecoverable. Save key offers a fast copy usable only on this Tab5, or a portable .t5key copy protected by a password of at least 12 characters. The portable copy takes longer and can be cancelled. To recover keys on another device, keep a portable copy and its password.

In Files, the padlock encrypts or decrypts a copy. Originals and ordinary editor backups remain readable. The vault protects selected files on a removed card; closing it does not protect every document or the device's internal memory.

Password vault stores up to 64 usernames, tokens or passwords under variable names. New, Save and Delete manage entries. Show / hide changes field visibility; Copy keeps the value in the clipboard for 30 seconds. The terminal, MicroPython and applications can read these values while the vault is unlocked. Git can reference two entries for the username and token. A program can retain or disclose a value it has already received, even after locking; use trusted programs.␀␀␀The vault requires a 4 to 12 digit PIN on first use. Changing it requires the current PIN; an already open session is not sufficient. Locking or turning off the screen closes the session. The PIN protects access in the interface and does not replace a portable key backup.

The legacy vault is preserved. Its original password is still required to recover its keys, and opening it may take time. In Vault access, Open legacy vault followed by Copy keys to device vault migrates the keys without deleting the original keyring. Creating a new device vault does not decrypt older files when their key is missing.

