help [command]   pwd   cd [directory]   ls [-al] [directory]
cat file...   head/tail [-n count] file...   wc file...
grep [-in] text file...   find [directory] [-name pattern]
mkdir [-p] path...   rmdir path...   touch path...
cp source destination   mv source destination   rm [-r] path...
echo [-n] text...   printf format [text...]   clear
set name value   unset name   env   test   true   false
sh/source file.sh [arguments...]   date   df   sleep seconds
memory   uptime   wifi   sha256 file...

Paths are relative to the current SD directory. Quote spaces.
Wildcards: * ? [abc]. Variables: $name ${name} $PWD $?.
Separate commands with ; or a new line. Conditions: && and ||.
Redirect: > file or >> file. Errors stay on the console.
for f in /Documents/*.txt; do echo "$f"; done
Ctrl+C: copy selection, or interrupt when nothing is selected.
Up/Down: history. Tab: completion. No pipes, background jobs or Bash substitution.
