Display: timeouts %lu Â· errors %lu/%lu Â· code %ld␀␀␀␀  â€¢  active␀␀␀  â€¢  offline␀␀  â€¢  lightweight␀␀  â€¢  insufficient memory␀␀  â€¢  saved␀␀␀␀  â€¢  open␀  â€¢  secured␀␀  â€¢  Internet radio␀␀␀  â€¢  network deferred: memory busy␀␀␀␀ Â· pending␀%s â€” PSRAM free %u KiB, block %u KiB, request %u KiB␀␀%s â€” internal RAM free %u KiB, block %u KiB, request %u KiB␀␀␀%s â€” free SRAM %u KiB, block %u KiB, requested %u KiB␀/join #channel Â· /msg nickname text Â· /me text Â· /nick nickname Â· /part Â· /close Â· /quit␀␀A Â· touch active␀␀␀ANS: last result Â· MEM: memory␀AVI/MJPEG  â€¢  PCM audio␀␀␀AVI/MJPEG  â€¢  no PCM audio␀␀␀␀Local or HTTP(S) AVI/MJPEG  â€¢  P4 hardware decoding␀␀␀Home Â· Alt+1␀␀␀Home Â· F6␀␀Refresh Â· F5␀␀␀Shows HTTP status, verified HTTPS certificate and useful audit headers. -L follows up to 5 redirects; -T limits total time to 1â€“3600 seconds, default 120.␀␀␀␀Shows an HTTP response (up to 32 KiB), or saves it with -o file or -O (name from the URL). -I requests headers; -L follows redirects; -T limits total time to 1â€“3600 seconds, default 120. HTTPS verifies the certificate and hostname.␀␀␀Show hidden files Â· Ctrl+H␀Show images Â· Ctrl I␀␀␀South Africa Â· GMT+2␀␀␀Shortcut help Â· F1␀Help and shortcutsâ€¦␀␀␀USB power Â· no battery␀Analysis in progressâ€¦␀Analyze Â· Ctrl+Enter␀␀␀Old vault Â· password␀␀␀Undo Â· Ctrl+Z␀␀Pairing Bluetoothâ€¦␀␀␀␀Applications brings together built-in tools and applications installed on the SD card in one grid. Refresh scans the local catalogue; this is not an online store. Built-in tools remain available without an SD card.

From Home, Customize selects the default or custom layout, visible applications, their order and icons. Save keeps this choice on the Tab5. Back discards changes. Reset restores the default layout after Save; it does not delete files or applications. Settings remains accessible in the side dock.

For applications that offer Hide, that command or Escape keeps them running. The resume button in the top bar or Ctrl+Alt+P returns to a hidden application while it remains active. Stop or Ctrl+. requests its termination. When a previous application must stop before another can start, confirm the proposed switch.

Maps â†’ Download opens the area form with the current centre, zoom and map source. Choose a city or coordinates, radius and zoom levels, then check the estimate. OpenTopoMap downloads directly on the tablet; pause/resume keeps your progress. OpenStreetMap requires a source that allows these downloads or PC preparation. Return to Maps to view the result without restarting.

Wikipedia searches the SD card first, then offers online results. An existing local copy takes priority. After online reading, Save this page makes it available offline. Options groups automatic saving, updates and complete downloads with language selection. Downloading a new complete archive requires confirmation. The reader keeps portrait mode, text size and line spacing.

IRC Chat remembers your nickname and server. Channels lets you join, leave, add or remove favourites and find recent channels. Hide keeps the connection running. No message history is saved to the SD card; preferences remain in /System/irc.json.

Import Radio Stations searches Radio Browser. Wi-Fi and a correct date are required for secure connections.

In the Wikipedia reader, in-text links open other articles, checking local copies first. Back returns to the previous article. The Illustrations option embeds images in the page; saved copies retain downloaded images.␀␀Press â€˜Portrait readerâ€™ to begin.␀␀␀Stopping Bluetoothâ€¦␀␀␀Stop requested â€” waiting for cooperation␀␀Stoppingâ€¦␀Network stop pending â€” try again␀␀Stop Â· Ctrl+.␀␀Python workshop Â· Tab5␀Waiting for the printer to respondâ€¦␀␀␀No archives added. Options â†’ Add a ZIM archive from the SD card.␀␀No key â€” create one in Settings␀␀␀No recent reading â€” choose a document␀Sydney, Australia Â· GMT+10/+11␀Another languageâ€¦␀Other applicationsâ€¦␀␀␀Azimuth Â· Â°␀␀␀B Â· touch paused␀␀␀Unsupported BMP (uncompressed 24/32-bit, â‰¤8192).␀␀Observed band: 240 kHz Â· automatic gain␀␀␀␀Battery: %.2f V Â· %+ld mA
%s␀␀␀MicroPython libraries Â· all boards␀Librariesâ€¦␀␀␀␀Compatible binary â€” ready to install␀␀SÃ£o Paulo, Brazil Â· GMT-3␀C Â· Animated LVGL␀␀Counting pagesâ€¦␀␀␀Calculate Â· Enter␀␀Toronto, Canada Â· GMT-5/-4␀Capturing the displayed mapâ€¦␀␀SD card unavailable â€” Maps could not open␀Map Â· Enter: move with arrows Â· +/âˆ’: zoom Â· Home: home position Â· Escape: controls␀␀␀␀Map Â· Arrows: move Â· +/âˆ’: zoom Â· I: information Â· Home: home location Â· Esc: controls␀␀␀␀Encryptingâ€¦␀␀␀China Â· GMT+8␀␀Choose a Python scriptâ€¦␀␀␀Choose an ELF applicationâ€¦␀␀␀␀Choose a radio category, album or recording, then an item to play. On a keyboard, Up/Down select and Enter plays. Space toggles play / pause; Alt+Left / Right selects the previous / next track. These keys retain their normal use in text fields.

Configure Wi-Fi in Settings. Stations come from /radios.json, albums from /Audio, and videos from /Video or /videos.json. Supported video formats are AVI/MJPEG and raw MJPEG. Escape leaves full-screen video.

Changing apps can leave audio playing. Use Pause or Stop to end playback. Startup and playback errors are reported. No periodic memory check clears applications or interrupts the radio. Settings â†’ System shows available resources.

The magnifying glass or Ctrl+F filters the active tab: tracks from all albums, stations from all radio categories, recordings or videos. Each tab keeps its own search words. The cross clears the filter; choosing a result plays the matching item. Names, folders and categories can be searched regardless of Latin case or accents.

Music browses subfolders of /Audio and /mp3. + in the left panel creates a subcategory. For radio, a category such as Jazz/Piano creates two levels. + on a track or station adds a favorite; the checkmark removes it. Favorites filters the current tab. Favorites are saved on the SD card.␀␀␀Choose a radio category, album or recording, then an item to play. On a keyboard, Up/Down select and Enter plays. Space toggles play / pause; Alt+Left / Right selects the previous / next track. These keys retain their normal use in text fields.

Configure Wi-Fi in Settings. Stations come from /radios.json, albums from /Audio, and videos from /Video or /videos.json. Supported video formats are AVI/MJPEG and raw MJPEG. Escape leaves full-screen video.

Changing apps can leave audio playing. Use Pause or Stop to end playback. Startup and playback errors are reported. No periodic memory check clears applications or interrupts the radio. Settings â†’ System shows available resources.

The magnifying glass or Ctrl+F filters the active tab: tracks from all albums, stations from all radio categories, recordings or videos. Each tab keeps its own search words. The cross clears the filter; choosing a result plays the matching item. Names, folders and categories can be searched regardless of Latin case or accents.

Music browses subfolders of /Audio and /mp3. The + on the left creates a subcategory. A radio category such as Jazz/Piano creates two levels. The star adds or removes a favourite. The Favourites selector filters the list; favourites remain saved on the SD card.

Volume, including zero, is retained after restarting. Media restores the tab, Favourites filter and last selection without starting playback.␀Declared target â€” compatibility untested␀␀Keyboard Â· F1␀␀Keys copied â€” legacy vault preserved␀␀Code: %06lu Â· read-only Â· %lu min␀Device vault unreadable â€” legacy vault preserved␀␀Paste selection Â· Ctrl+V␀␀␀Paste Â· Ctrl+V␀Start writingâ€¦␀␀␀␀Countingâ€¦␀Connecting Bluetoothâ€¦␀Connecting securelyâ€¦␀␀Encrypted copy created â€” original kept␀␀␀␀Copy selection Â· Ctrl+C␀␀␀␀Copy Â· 30 s␀␀␀␀Copy Â· Ctrl+C␀␀Text and background colour Â· Ctrl+Shift+C␀␀Colour and highlightingâ€¦␀␀Cut selection Â· Ctrl+X␀Cut Â· Ctrl+X␀␀␀Create a project with this documentâ€¦␀␀Create a theme: select a color from the list or touch an object in the preview. Adjust R, G and B, or enter #RRGGBB, then save.

In Files, select a file and choose Open withâ€¦ to pick a program from Applications. The launcher includes file and folder pickers, recent items and favorites. Run starts the program; Ctrl+. stops it.

Game Boy and Game Boy Color: arrows control the D-pad; Z and X are A and B; Enter is Start; Backspace is Select. Escape exits and saves. The disk button saves without exiting; the circular arrow restarts. Open .gb or .gbc ROM files from Files. Saves and states are kept under /Saves/GB and /Saves/GBC. The latest compatible state resumes when the ROM is reopened.␀␀Create a theme is a native tool: select a color from the list or by touching a preview object. Adjust R, G and B, or enter #RRGGBB, then save. Its widgets and buffers are released when you close it.

In Files, select a file, choose Open withâ€¦ and select an .app.elf from Applications. The launcher also offers file and folder pickers, recent items and favorites. Run starts the program; Ctrl+. requests a stop.

Game Boy: arrow keys and the physical Z/X keys control the D-pad and A/B. Enter = Start, Backspace = Select. Escape exits and saves state. The disk button saves without exiting; the circular arrow restarts the game. Saves and states are in /Saves/GB. The latest compatible state resumes when you reopen the ROM.␀␀␀Create a theme: choose a colour from the list or by touching an object in the preview. Adjust R, G and B or enter #RRGGBB, then save. The Black / White slider darkens or lightens the colour symmetrically; at the centre it preserves the starting colour.

In Explorer, select a file, then Open withâ€¦ and choose a compatible ELF application. The launcher also offers a file and folder picker, recent items and favourites. Run starts the program; Ctrl+. requests it to stop.

Game Boy: arrow keys and physical Z/X keys control the directional pad and A/B. Enter = Start, Backspace = Select. Escape exits and saves the state. The floppy-disk button saves without exiting; the circular arrow restarts the game. .gb files open Game Boy; .gbc files open Game Boy Color. Saves and states are in /Saves/GB or /Saves/GBC. The last compatible state resumes when the ROM is next opened.␀Create a theme: choose a colour from the list or by touching an object in the preview. Adjust R, G and B or enter #RRGGBB, then save. The Black / White slider darkens or lightens the colour symmetrically; at the centre it preserves the starting colour.

In Explorer, select a file, then Open withâ€¦ and choose a compatible ELF application. The launcher also offers a file and folder picker, recent items and favourites. Run starts the program; Ctrl+. requests it to stop.

Game Boy: arrow keys and physical Z/X keys control the directional pad and A/B. Enter = Start, Backspace = Select. Escape exits and saves the state. The floppy-disk button saves without exiting; the circular arrow restarts the game. .gb files open Game Boy; .gbc files open Game Boy Color. Saves and states are in /Saves/GB or /Saves/GBC. The last compatible state resumes when the ROM is next opened.

A USB HID or XInput controller also operates the OS: directional pad to navigate, A to confirm, B to go back. In MicroPython, the gamepad.py module provides state(). capture(True) reserves input for the script while its interface is in the foreground; capture(False) restores OS navigation.␀D Â· OS screen␀␀LIVE  â€¢  %02lu:%02lu␀␀In Explorer, Up/Down select, Enter opens and Backspace goes up. One click selects; a double click or second tap opens. For images, this shows the preview on the right; tapping the preview or image icon opens the viewer. Copy/Cut prepares the item; Paste acts in the current folder.

System files remain accessible for updating data. Amber colouring indicates their role; hidden items are dimmed. Changing or deleting a configuration, language, font or catalogue can affect Tab5OS: keep a copy before making your own changes.

Save stores the document; Save as chooses its name and folder. Explorer updates after changes; F5 refreshes it, Ctrl+H shows hidden items, and Hide changes the selection's hidden state without renaming files. Previews count all visible items; previous backups remain in .Tab5Backups. Keep the storage connected while writing.

File names and document text are personal data: changing the interface language does not translate them.

The magnifying glass or Ctrl+F searches file and folder names in the current folder and all its subfolders. Case and Latin accents are ignored; all search words must be present. Results appear progressively with their folder. Partial searches are indicated: refine the words if necessary. The cross appears only during a search and removes the filter. Text and source files, including .py scripts, open in Writing without running automatically.

A .bin file opens the Firmware page. Verify checks the ESP32-P4 target, revision, size and fingerprint. Install writes to the inactive partition and validates the image before changing the next boot target. Restart activates it. Use an application binary made for this Tab5, without a bootloader or partition table. Keep the power supply stable.

Menus group actions and their shortcuts. Sort by selects name, date or size in either direction. Right-click opens contextual actions. Open in terminal uses the current folder.

Open or Run on a .sh script starts the terminal in the scriptâ€™s folder. To edit it, use Open with.␀␀Request stop Â· Ctrl+.␀␀Display diagnostic Â· Ctrl+Alt+D␀␀␀␀Right document Â· Enter: browse Â· Escape: controls␀Whole document Â· no Markdown headings␀␀Right-hand documentsâ€¦␀Parent folder Â· Backspace␀␀Directory â€” kept␀␀Double buffering: %s
Timeouts: %lu Â· errors: %lu
