Uptime %u min Â· startup %lu ms␀␀␀␀Clear output Â· Ctrl+L␀␀Waiting for Wi-Fiâ€¦␀␀␀␀Encoding JPEGâ€¦␀␀␀␀Text encodingâ€¦␀␀␀␀Saving text for printingâ€¦␀Save report Â· Ctrl+S␀␀␀Save as Â· Ctrl+Shift+S␀Save asâ€¦␀␀Commit the repositoryâ€™s entire index␀␀Save Â· Ctrl+S␀␀Enter: activate Â· Escape: back␀Enter: open Â· Up/Down: select Â· Backspace: parent folder␀␀Enter opens the selected setting, arrows adjust its value and Escape returns to the controls. In Settings â†’ Interface â†’ Display, the Theme list applies immediately and Corner radius adjusts control shapes; brightness and text size remain independent.

Packs in /System/languages/*.json define the interface language, including help and messages. French also uses its SD pack when present. Missing translations fall back to English, except French retains the source label.

If the SD font is missing or cannot load, the interface temporarily switches to English with the built-in font. The selected language remains saved. Restarting with an available font restores that language; documents are never translated or changed. Also restart after editing language packs to reload them.

The keyboard can follow the interface language or be chosen separately in Settings â†’ Language; the fifteen supplied layouts apply to both touch and USB keyboards. Chinese uses pinyin, Japanese uses romaji/kana with candidate selection, and Korean uses Hangul composition; Ctrl+Space switches to and from Latin input.

A compatible font must contain the languageâ€™s characters. Date, time, time zone, NTP and Wi-Fi have their own settings. F1 remains available to return to this help.

Without a detected USB keyboard, touching an input opens the on-screen keyboard. With a USB keyboard, it stays closed automatically; its button can open it manually. The down arrow always closes it; Enter also closes it in a single-line field.␀␀␀Enter opens the selected setting, arrows adjust its value and Escape returns to the controls. In Settings â†’ Interface â†’ Display, the Theme list applies immediately and Corner radius adjusts control shapes; brightness and text size remain independent.

Packs in /System/languages/*.json define the interface language, including help and messages. French also uses its SD pack when present. Missing translations fall back to English, except French retains the source label.

If the SD font is missing or cannot load, the interface temporarily switches to English with the built-in font. The selected language remains saved. Restarting with an available font restores that language; documents are never translated or changed. Also restart after editing language packs to reload them.

Choose the keyboard separately in Settings â†’ Language. The fifteen layouts apply to touch and USB keyboards. Chinese uses pinyin, Japanese romaji/kana and Korean Hangul composition; Ctrl+Space switches to and from Latin input.

A compatible font must contain the languageâ€™s characters. Date, time, time zone, NTP and Wi-Fi have their own settings. F1 remains available to return to this help.

Without a detected USB keyboard, touching an input opens the on-screen keyboard. With a USB keyboard, it stays closed automatically; its button can open it manually. The down arrow always closes it; Enter also closes it in a single-line field.␀Sending interrupted â€” check the printer queue before retrying␀Sending to printerâ€¦␀␀␀Native application error â€” see console␀␀␀␀Run application Â· Ctrl+Enter␀␀␀FM 87.5â€“108 MHz␀␀␀Close help Â· F1 / Escape␀␀␀Close Â· Escape␀Closing USB connectionâ€¦␀␀␀File â†’ Print (Ctrl+P) saves the document and opens printing. In Explorer, the printer icon appears for a selected file, never a folder. Search queries IPP/IPPS advertisements on the local Wi-Fi network. Selecting a result uses its advertised port and queue path. An unadvertised printer can still be reached by entering its exact address. Enter or the on-screen keyboardâ€™s down arrow closes the keyboard. Check queries the printer without printing.

HTTP 426 requests a protocol upgrade, often TLS. Search may provide the IPPS address; Try IPPS tests a secure connection to the same host and port without sending a document. The certificate can be validated using /System/printer-ca.pem. Otherwise, compare the SHA-256 fingerprint with the printerâ€™s before trusting it. It is checked on every connection; a change blocks sending.

Choose A4, Letter or A5, orientation, resolution and a size from 25 to 200 %. At 100 %, photos and maps fit the printable area; enlargements may span several sheets. For text, the percentage changes font size and pagination. Pages are estimated before sending; a resolution adjusted to the printer may change rounding. Markdown images are separated from text; tables print as text. The printer must accept IPP and sRGB color PWG Raster. USB printing is unavailable. Cancelling during sending may leave a job in the printer queue: check before resending.

Calculator: digits, + - * /, parentheses, powers and Â² work on the physical keyboard. Enter or = calculates; Backspace corrects. MS stores the result, MR inserts MEM, M+/Mâˆ’ accumulate it, MC clears it. Degree/radian trigonometry, pi, ANS and unit conversions are available.

If HTTP 426 advertises Upgrade: TLS, verification now negotiates OPTIONS then TLS on the same HTTP connection. The advertised IPP address can therefore still be correct. Certificates are verified before sending any document. The engine must negotiate a compatible TLS version; a printer restricted to legacy TLS 1.0 can still fail. Print jobs are never resent automatically after an error.

The printer list and last selected address are saved in the Tab5, including across restarts. Only Search runs discovery again. A successful scan replaces the list; a network error retains the previous one. A manually entered address is saved after checking, printing or closing.

The printer button in the Editor toolbar saves the document and opens Print, just like Ctrl+P. If HTTP-to-TLS upgrade fails, diagnostics now show the printerâ€™s HTTP response; a positive socket number is no longer presented as a cryptographic error.␀File â†’ Open on right adds a text to the reference collection. Click the path in either pane to choose a heading. In the right path popup, the list at the top also lets you switch documents. It is for reading; open a file on the left to edit it.

Each pane has its own passage and heading arrows. The path beside the filename shows your position. The outline marks the active heading. Another upward swipe after reaching the bottom opens the next passage.

A link [profile](Notes.md#characters) reaches a heading on the right. Wikilinks [[Characters]], [[Notes#Characters]] and [[Characters|the profile]] search the collection. Multiple results offer a choice. Wikilinks are a convention, not universal Markdown syntax.

Documents are displayed in passages. The index may still be building after opening. A selection cannot cross a passage change. Reload the right pane after saving changes to its source.␀␀Finishing moveâ€¦␀␀␀Finland Â· GMT+2/+3␀Firmware installed â€” restart to activate␀␀Firmware Â· flash partition␀Waiting for MJPEG streamâ€¦␀MP3/AAC stream unavailable â€” touch to retry␀␀␀Stream interrupted â€” retry scheduled␀␀Radio stream unavailable â€” touch to retry␀Arrows / Page: change page
