Escape: quit Â· F1: hide help␀␀␀␀Format â†’ Color settings (Ctrl+Shift+C) chooses text and background colors separately. Choosing a swatch does not change the document. Text color (Ctrl+Alt+C) and Text background (Ctrl+Alt+H) affect the selection, or subsequent typing if nothing is selected. Table cells support these styles too. Escape closes the palette. The keyboard button is directly on the Editor toolbar and in the table editor. L+ and C+ immediately show the new row or column; Apply saves the table into the document.

JPG now captures the map already displayed at its current resolution, without increasing zoom or downloading more tiles. Wait until the desired details are visible before capturing. Credits remain below the image. The file is created in /Picture/Maps/map-NNNN.jpg.

A small panel keeps progress visible during copying and encoding. The cross or Escape cancels; changing the view during copying also cancels that stage. JPEG encoding runs by scanlines. No incomplete file is published. Writing â†’ Insert â†’ Image inserts the result.

Table cells keep visible borders; the active cell keeps a theme tint.␀␀␀␀Formatting USB â€” do not unplug␀␀␀␀USB formatting failed â€” drive not mounted␀Formattingâ€¦ Do not remove the USB drive.␀␀Formatâ€¦␀␀␀Frequency: 24â€“1766 MHz, depending on tuner␀␀␀␀Drag selection Â· Arrows: 1 px Â· Shift+arrows: 10 px␀␀␀Bold Â· Ctrl+B␀␀HTTP 426: find the printerâ€™s IPPS address␀Height Â· px␀␀␀␀Time set â€” RTC unavailable␀␀␀␀Credential saved Â· environment full␀␀␀␀MJPEG image invalid or larger than 1280Ã—720␀␀␀␀Importing folderâ€¦␀Import a folderâ€¦␀␀Import an SD image Â· Ctrl+Shift+I␀␀Print selected file Â· Ctrl+P␀␀␀Print Â· Ctrl+P␀India Â· GMT+5:30␀␀␀Local index missing Â· saved places and Mesh only␀␀␀Local index unreadable Â· saved places and Mesh only␀␀␀␀Local index unavailable Â· saved places and Mesh only␀␀␀Indexing documentâ€¦ Â· displayed passage available␀Indexingâ€¦␀Info at center Â· Hold to choose a point␀␀␀␀Point information Â· I: map centre␀␀System information Â· Tab5OS %s␀Installing firmwareâ€¦␀␀Insert / edit a table Â· Ctrl+T␀Intensity Â· %␀␀Querying printerâ€¦␀Italic Â· Ctrl+I␀␀␀␀Japan Â· GMT+9␀␀The gear opens the tool options. Edit offers copy, cut, paste and delete selection; repeated moves preserve the background. Inserted text uses the OS font.

Relief shades existing colours without changing their transparency. It simulates a surface, without creating 3D geometry. On a disc, Linear gives a conical profile and Circular a rounded profile; on other shapes they follow the boundary. Extrusion gives a constant height.

Profile width is set in pixels or as a proportion of the maximum distance to the boundary: at 100 %, it reaches the points furthest from the edge. Lower values leave a plateau. This setting does not apply to Extrusion.

Positive height: raised; negative: recessed. The light azimuth turns through 360Â°: 0Â° right, 90Â° down, 180Â° left, 270Â° up. Intensity controls lighting contrast; zero preserves the colours.␀␀␀␀Document languageâ€¦␀␀␀␀Wikipedia language (en, fr, de, esâ€¦)␀␀Language saved â€” restart to apply it everywhere␀␀␀The screen timeout dims then turns off the backlight. The tablet and any radio keep running, so this display sleep still uses battery power. A key or touch wakes the screen. To turn the tablet off, use its power button as described by M5Stack.

On Tab5, USB charging requires the tablet to be powered on and initialized. Turning off the screen does not turn off the tablet. The percentage alone cannot diagnose a battery; also check voltage, current and charge status. Without a battery, leave Battery installed off in Settings â†’ System â†’ Energy: the indicator stays USB, with no percentage or charging bolt. Enable it after installing a pack with the device powered off. This setting only controls the display, not the charger.

Settings â†’ System shows memory resources. The readout is passive: no automatic cache purge or periodic notification changes the screen. The last reset cause and serial logs help distinguish a memory error, a lockup and a voltage drop.

To report a problem, note the version, apps used, file sizes, preceding actions and the displayed message.␀␀The screen timeout dims then turns off the backlight. The tablet and any radio keep running, so this display sleep still uses battery power. A key or touch wakes the screen. To turn the tablet off, use its power button as described by M5Stack.

On Tab5, USB charging requires the tablet to be powered on and initialized. Turning off the screen does not turn off the tablet. The percentage alone cannot diagnose a battery; also check voltage, current and charge status. Without a battery, leave Battery installed off in Settings â†’ System â†’ Energy: the indicator stays USB, with no percentage or charging bolt. Enable it after installing a pack with the device powered off. This setting only controls the display, not the charger.

Settings â†’ System shows memory resources. The readout is passive: no automatic cache purge or periodic notification changes the screen. The last reset cause and serial logs help distinguish a memory error, a lockup and a voltage drop.

To report a problem, note the version, apps used, file sizes, preceding actions and the displayed message.

Battery monitoring uses pack voltage and current, not the percentage. A persistently low battery triggers a warning; a critical voltage starts a countdown followed by power-off. Plug in the tablet and save your work. Detected charging or an invalid reading cancels the countdown. This software protection does not guarantee recovery of a pack whose protection has already tripped. Charging requires the tablet to be powered on and initialized.␀Loading credentialsâ€¦␀␀Reading Meshtastic nodesâ€¦␀Reading headingsâ€¦␀Reading the Meshtastic serviceâ€¦␀␀␀Portrait reader Â· vertical scrolling␀␀␀Reading Â· F1␀␀␀Free: %.1f MiB Â· external memory␀␀␀Free: %u KiB Â· excluding cache and reservations␀␀␀␀Free: %u KiB Â· largest block: %u KiB␀␀␀Releasing caches for printingâ€¦␀␀␀␀Limit of 8 keys reached â€” legacy vault preserved␀␀EPUB book â€” open it to start reading.␀Home keeps built-in tools; the ELF and Python icons each open a dedicated application menu. Applications in each menu are sorted by name. Built-in tools remain available without an SD card. F5 refreshes the catalogue; this is not an online store.

Settings â†’ Interface â†’ Display â†’ Home and sidebar opens sidebar and home customization; without the sidebar, Home remains at the top, and Alt+7 always opens Settings. Customize home sets applications, order, icons, grid or list, size and labels: Save keeps your choices, Back discards them, and Reset followed by Save restores the initial layout without deleting files.

Exiting a Python application closes its screen and returns to the previous OS screen. For applications offering Hide, that command keeps execution running. The sidebar resume button or Ctrl+Alt+P restores a hidden application while it remains active. Stop or Ctrl+. requests it to stop. When another application needs to stop before launching, confirm the proposed switch.

Maps â†’ Download opens the area form with the current centre, zoom and map background. Choose a city or coordinates, radius and zooms, then check the estimate. OpenTopoMap downloads directly on the tablet; pause/resume keeps progress. OpenStreetMap requires a source that allows these downloads or preparation on a PC. Return to Maps to view the result without restarting.

Wikipedia presents local and online results in the same pagination, without isolating a local result on its own page. An existing local copy takes priority. After reading online, Save this page makes it available offline. Options groups automatic saving, updates and complete downloads with language selection. A new complete archive requires confirmation before downloading. The reader keeps portrait orientation, text size and line spacing.

IRC Chat remembers nickname and server. Channels lets you join, leave, add or remove favourites and find recent channels. Hide keeps the connection. No message history is stored on the SD card; preferences remain in /System/irc.json.

Import radios uses Radio Browser. Wi-Fi and a correct date are required for secure connections.

In the Wikipedia reader, text links open other articles, searching local copies first. Backspace or Escape returns to results; Alt+Left also goes back. Illustrations in the reading toolbar shows or hides images. A local result's menu lets you delete the displayed copy or archive after confirmation. Tables keep their cells and horizontal scrolling.␀The Writing editor opens Python files and other source code, preserving raw text and displaying syntax colors. The Code menu provides Run, Stop, Resume, Libraries and the console on the right. Ctrl+Enter saves and runs the Python file. Ctrl+. stops it.

The Documents menu keeps your open-file list even when buffers are released. The cross removes an entry without deleting its file. Switching first saves changes; a failed save keeps the current document.

Create a project from a document, add more files or import a folder. Imported folders are scanned progressively while the editor is visible. New files appear automatically; explicitly removed entries stay excluded. Standalone files remain available outside projects.

Libraries opens the MicroPython catalogue, with target-board selection and modules added to the corresponding project. Libraries for another board stay separate from the Tab5 modules; their hardware drivers are not executed on the Tab5. Declared compatibility does not guarantee operation on a particular board. CPython packages and native CPython extensions are incompatible. Automatic upload or flashing of another board is not provided.

Bundled scripts remain in /MicroPython. Check SD card compares resources before repair, preserves personal files and backs up each replaced file.

Open withâ€¦ selects an Application for a document or ROM. Applications execute from SD without replacing the firmware; stopping is cooperative. Native code shares OS memory. A .bin is still a firmware update.␀␀␀␀Headroom: %u KiB Â· total flash: %u MiB␀Hide images Â· Ctrl I␀␀␀Hide or unhide selection Â· Ctrl+Shift+H␀␀␀␀Hide Â· Ctrl+Alt+P to resume␀␀␀␀Meshtastic Â· New message␀␀␀Laying outâ€¦␀␀␀Modified â€” kept␀␀␀Cannot mount USB â€” reconnect the drive␀␀␀␀Not enough memory for radio â€” close an app then retry␀Not enough memory â€” use search␀␀␀␀Memory busy â€” retry after caches are released␀New Zealand Â· GMT+12/+13␀␀␀NTP enabled â€” waiting for Wi-Fi␀␀␀NTP disabled â€” RTC clock␀␀Variable name Â· letters, digits and _␀␀New PIN â€” 4 to 12 digits␀␀New document Â· Ctrl+N␀␀Git operation in progressâ€¦␀␀␀␀Opening videoâ€¦␀␀␀␀Unlocking vaultâ€¦␀␀Opening video streamâ€¦␀Openingâ€¦␀␀Open withâ€¦␀␀␀␀Open main.py in Writing. Add its folder to the editor's projects with Documents â†’ Import a folder.␀␀␀␀Open Â· Ctrl+O␀␀Open on rightâ€¦␀␀␀␀Openâ€¦␀Optional PIN Â· 4 to 12 digits␀␀PSRAM Â· heap␀␀␀Page loaded Â· simplified reading␀␀␀Reading pages Â· no JavaScript␀␀Estimated pages: â€¦␀␀␀␀Active partition Â· remaining: %u KiB␀␀␀Customâ€¦␀␀␀Document outlineâ€¦␀Outline unavailable Â· whole document␀␀␀Several headings match â€” choose a document␀␀␀␀OS font Â· Enter applies Â· Shift+Enter: new line Â· Escape cancels␀Fonts and textâ€¦␀␀␀Profile width Â· %␀␀Profile width Â· px␀Preparing map for paperâ€¦␀␀Preparing copyâ€¦␀␀␀Preparing pagesâ€¦␀␀Preparing high-resolution JPEGâ€¦␀␀␀Starting or closing file sharingâ€¦␀Exit Â· Escape␀␀UK Â· GMT+0/+1␀␀Radio stopped: critical memory level â€” free memory then retry␀Radio stopped after three failures â€” touch to retry␀␀␀Collect three yellow keys, then reach the green exit.
Arrows: move and turn Â· X/B: run
Backspace / Select: map Â· Enter / Start: new maze
Page up/down: volume Â· Ctrl+S: save
Escape: exit Â· F1: hide help␀␀␀Searching for printersâ€¦␀␀␀Scanning Wi-Fi networksâ€¦␀␀Searching for placeâ€¦␀␀Looking for tunerâ€¦␀␀␀␀Searching for Meshtastic devicesâ€¦␀Scanningâ€¦␀Search Â© OpenStreetMap contributors␀␀␀␀Find / replace â€” whole document, case-sensitive␀␀␀Find / replaceâ€¦␀␀␀Search Â· Ctrl+F␀␀␀␀Findâ€¦␀Searchingâ€¦␀␀␀␀SD reconnecting â€” try again␀␀␀Reconnecting to live MJPEGâ€¦␀␀␀Reconnecting radioâ€¦␀␀␀Fillingâ€¦␀␀Restoring documentâ€¦␀␀␀Restoring keyâ€¦␀␀␀␀Back Â· Backspace / Escape␀␀Back Â· Esc␀Back to home Â· Backspace␀␀␀Return to preview Â· Esc␀␀␀␀Rotate screen 180Â°␀Reopen with an encodingâ€¦␀␀Color settingsâ€¦␀␀␀Settings â†’ Storage opens the microSD and USB controls, even without an SD card. Mount / retest microSD restarts detection; Open microSD goes to the root /. A compatible USB drive or card reader can mount automatically; this option can be disabled. USB files appear under /USB. Copy, paste, create, rename and delete work on both drives.

Save documents and stop applications or transfers using the drive before Eject microSD or Eject USB. An operation in progress may prevent ejection. Wait for confirmation before removing the card or unplugging the drive. One USB drive can be mounted at a time, alongside a keyboard and mouse on the hub. FAT16/FAT32 are supported.

Missing resources progressively recreates missing standard system files from the firmware. Cancel repair interrupts this work. Existing files, documents and customisations are preserved. This function does not replace damaged files already present and does not recover deleted files. Fonts, encyclopaedias and .app.elf applications must still be supplied separately.

Without a usable SD font, the interface temporarily uses English and the built-in font, without changing the saved language or your document text. Restarting with the font restores the selected language. This version offers neither formatting nor recovery of erased data.␀␀Settings â†’ Storage opens the microSD and USB controls, even without an SD card. Reconnect microSD restarts detection; Open in the microSD panel goes to the root /. A compatible USB drive or card reader can mount automatically; this option can be disabled. USB files appear under /USB. Copy, paste, create, rename and delete work on both drives.

Save documents and stop applications or transfers using the drive before choosing Eject in the driveâ€™s panel. An operation in progress may prevent ejection. Wait for confirmation before removing the card or unplugging the drive. One USB drive can be mounted at a time, alongside a keyboard and mouse on the hub. FAT16/FAT32 are supported.

Restore missing files progressively recreates missing standard system files from the firmware. Cancel interrupts this work. Existing files, documents and customisations are preserved. This function does not replace damaged files already present and does not recover deleted files. Fonts, encyclopaedias and .app.elf applications must still be supplied separately.

Without a usable SD font, the interface temporarily uses English and the built-in font, without changing the saved language or your document text. Restarting with the font restores the selected language. This version offers neither formatting nor recovery of erased data.␀␀Settings â†’ System â†’ SD card over Wi-Fi opens temporary read/write sharing. Current network uses your existing Wi-Fi: the PC must be on the same network. Direct network creates temporary Wi-Fi; first turn off the OS Wi-Fi, then connect the PC using the displayed name and password.

Open the displayed address in the PC browser and enter the code. No additional software is needed. The browser lets you browse, download, upload, rename and delete files, and create folders. Sharing stops after 30 minutes or with Stop.

Keep the card inserted during a transfer and avoid editing the same file in an application. Stop sharing before changing Wi-Fi. This is browser access; the card does not appear as a USB drive letter in Windows.␀␀␀Settings â†’ System â†’ Sharing opens a temporary read/write share. Current network uses your existing Wi-Fi: the PC must be on the same network. Direct network creates a temporary Wi-Fi network; first disable the OS Wi-Fi, then connect the PC using the displayed name and password.

Open the displayed address in the PC browser and enter the code. No extra software is needed. The browser lets you browse, download, upload, rename and delete files, and create folders. Sharing stops after 30 minutes or with Stop.

During a transfer, leave the card in place and avoid editing the same file in an application. Stop sharing before changing Wi-Fi. This is browser access; the card does not appear as a USB drive letter in Windows.␀␀␀␀Late response after sending â€” check the printer queue␀Network: %s Â· password: %s
Browser: %s Â· code: %06lu
