The heap is memory available for allocation. Firmware is stored in flash.␀␀␀HP SRAM Â· heap␀Enter the frequency in kHz or MHz; the touch keypad accepts a decimal point. Ranges are suggestions and can be changed: the dongle determines accepted frequencies and inputs. AM, WFM and NFM are modes, not frequency limits.

Apply changes settings during reception; the âˆ’/+ buttons use the selected step. The spectrum has separate controls for X span and offset, Y minimum and maximum. dBFS levels are relative, without power calibration.

In Scan, set the range, step, dwell and threshold, then Scan. Pause/Resume stops or continues the scan; Hold keeps the frequency for listening. Detections holds up to 2048 entries in pages of 24. Listen tunes to a frequency; Delete/Clear changes the list, then Save stores it in /System/SDR/detections.csv. The threshold does not identify the station.

In WFM, mono audio filters out stereo and RDS components. De-emphasis is generally 50 Âµs in Europe or 75 Âµs depending on the country. Correction (ppm) compensates for the dongleâ€™s oscillator error; start at 0 and adjust using a known frequency. A suitable antenna and sufficient radio signal are still needed.␀␀␀␀Enter the frequency in kHz or MHz; the touch keypad accepts a decimal point. Ranges are suggestions and can be changed: the dongle determines accepted frequencies and inputs. AM, WFM and NFM are modes, not frequency limits.

Apply changes settings during reception; the âˆ’/+ buttons use the selected step. The spectrum has separate controls for X span and offset, Y minimum and maximum. dBFS levels are relative, without power calibration.

Set start, end, step, duration and threshold, then Scan range. Scanning makes one pass of up to 20,000 steps and can pause on a signal. Hold frequency keeps the tuned frequency. Up to 128 detections can be received again, deleted and saved to /System/SDR/detections.csv. Saving also preserves deletions. The threshold does not identify a station by name.␀␀␀␀Enter the frequency in kHz or MHz; the touch keypad accepts a decimal point. Ranges are suggestions and can be changed: the dongle determines accepted frequencies and inputs. AM, WFM and NFM are modes, not frequency limits.

Apply changes settings during reception; the âˆ’/+ buttons use the selected step. The spectrum has separate controls for X span and offset, Y minimum and maximum. dBFS levels are relative, without power calibration.

Set start, end, step, duration and threshold, then Scan range. Scanning makes one pass of up to 20,000 steps and can pause on a signal. Hold frequency keeps the tuned frequency. Up to 128 detections can be received again, deleted and saved to /System/SDR/detections.csv. Saving also preserves deletions. The threshold does not identify a station by name.

In WFM, mono audio filters out stereo and RDS components. De-emphasis is generally 50 Âµs in Europe or 75 Âµs depending on the country. Correction (ppm) compensates for the dongleâ€™s oscillator error; start at 0 and adjust using a known frequency. A suitable antenna and sufficient radio signal are still needed.␀No subfolder  â€¢  /Audio␀␀␀No subfolder  â€¢  /mp3␀Backing up keyâ€¦␀␀␀Script runningâ€¦␀␀␀IMAP server Â· TLS 993␀␀IRC server Â· verified TLS connection␀␀␀SMTP server Â· TLS 465␀␀Audio output unavailable â€” stop playback then retry␀␀␀Spectrum active Â· audio output busy␀␀␀␀USB drive ejected â€” safe to remove␀␀␀␀In Map, select the map then press Enter to control it. Arrows move the view; + / âˆ’ changes zoom; Home returns to the home position. Escape returns arrows to navigation between controls. Ctrl+F opens search.

Saved places let you reach a position, rename it or delete it. Style selects the map background. Offline .t5map packs and the SD cache provide tiles already available. Online searches and missing tiles need a connection. Search results use the selected language when the service provides it.

Portrait reading opens a text or EPUB. Page Up / Page Down turns pages. Up/Down scroll when controls are not selected. Escape leaves reading or a full-screen image. Titles and names from your files keep their original language.␀␀On Map, select the map and press Enter to control it. Arrow keys move the view; + / âˆ’ changes zoom; Home goes to the home position. Escape returns the arrows to navigation between controls. Ctrl+F opens search.

Saved places let you visit, rename or delete a position. Style selects the map background. Offline .t5map packages and the SD cache let you view tiles already available. Online searches and missing tiles require a connection. Searched place names follow the selected language when the service provides it.

Portrait reading opens text or EPUB. Previous / next page, Left / Right and Up / Down turn EPUB pages when controls are not selected. Up / Down scrolls text. Backspace or Escape exits reading or the full-screen image. The percentage and page number refer to the entire book. A ~ sign indicates a provisional percentage during the first calculation; the total becomes exact when layout finishes. Titles and names supplied by your files keep their original language.␀␀␀On Map, select the map and press Enter to control it. Arrow keys move the view; + / âˆ’ changes zoom; Home goes to the home position. Escape returns the arrows to navigation between controls. Ctrl+F opens search.

Saved places let you visit, rename or delete a position. Style selects the map background. Offline .t5map packages and the SD cache let you view tiles already available. Online searches and missing tiles require a connection. Searched place names follow the selected language when the service provides it.

Portrait reading opens text or EPUB. Previous / next page, Left / Right and Up / Down turn EPUB pages when controls are not selected. Up / Down scrolls text. Backspace or Escape exits reading or the full-screen image. The percentage and page number refer to the entire book. A ~ sign indicates a provisional percentage during the first calculation; the total becomes exact when layout finishes. Titles and names supplied by your files keep their original language.

Remember last view saves position and zoom when leaving Maps, without writing on every movement. With this option disabled, the home position opens. A fresh installation uses a generic view.␀␀␀Selectingâ€¦␀␀␀␀Multiple selection Â· Space / Shift+arrows / Ctrl+A␀Tab5 Â· Local file sharing␀␀Tab5OS v%s Â· chip %u Â· SD %s Â· PSRAM %.1f MiB Â· %s␀␀Tab5OS v%s Â· chip %u Â· SD %s Â· free PSRAM %.1f MiB Â· %s␀Table â€” first row: headings␀␀␀Tableâ€¦␀␀␀␀Text size Â· %␀␀Actual size Â· 100 %␀␀␀␀Terminal â€” help␀␀␀SD test requested â€” wait for tasks to finish and stop media playback␀␀Text: Ctrl+Alt+C Â· Background: Ctrl+Alt+H␀␀Text Â· Enter: edit Â· Escape: controls␀Theme saved â€” applied after restart␀␀␀Touch the text to place the caret. Hold then drag to select characters; holding without dragging selects a word. A normal swipe scrolls. On a keyboard, Shift+arrows extends the selection.

Bold and Italic stay active while typing. With a selection, they change that selection; switching a style off removes it. Heading changes the current paragraph. Text and highlight colours are set in the palette.

Ctrl+S: save. Ctrl+Shift+S: save as. Ctrl+N / Ctrl+O: new / open. Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y: undo / redo. Ctrl+B / Ctrl+I: bold / italic. Ctrl+C / X / V: copy / cut / paste. Ctrl+F / Ctrl+H: find / replace.

Ctrl+A selects the whole document. Ctrl+Shift+Home/End extends the selection; Insert toggles overwrite mode. Page Up / Page Down changes passage; Ctrl+Home / End reaches the document ends. Escape leaves editing; select the text area then Enter to resume.

Display â†’ Serial opens communication on the port chosen in Settings. In Data mode, Send transmits the selection, or the whole document if nothing is selected. Listen receives text in a separate panel; Insert places it in the document. Collapsing the panel keeps listening active; leaving the editor stops its serial session. For binary files and stream redirection, use the terminal serial commands.␀␀␀Select all Â· Ctrl+A␀␀␀␀PNG tiles: 256 Ã— 256 required␀␀Downloads to SD or USB. -O chooses the file; otherwise its name comes from the URL. -L follows redirects; -T limits total time to 1â€“3600 seconds (default 120). --overwrite replaces a file after success.␀␀␀␀Chicago, USA Â· GMT-6/-5␀␀␀␀Denver, USA Â· GMT-7/-6␀Los Angeles, USA Â· GMT-8/-7␀␀␀␀New York, USA Â· GMT-5/-4␀␀␀USB Â· %llu MiB␀USB Â· %s Â· %llu MiB␀␀␀Previous version restored â€” Undo is still available␀␀␀Verifying copyâ€¦␀␀␀Verifying firmwareâ€¦␀␀␀Wi-Fi  â€¢  connectingâ€¦␀␀␀Wi-Fi enabled  â€¢  no network␀␀Wi-Fi enabled â€” choose a network␀␀microSD Â· %llu MiB␀Â© OpenStreetMap contributors Â· Nominatim search␀␀␀âˆ’: recessed Â· +: raised␀␀âˆ’: inward Â· +: around the edge␀␀␀/?#␀[MAP] allocation PSRAM des tables impossible␀␀␀␀Â© OpenStreetMap contributors␀␀␀https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png␀␀osm␀osm-fast␀␀␀␀Â© OpenStreetMap Â· SRTM Â· OpenTopoMap (CC-BY-SA)␀␀https://tile.opentopomap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png␀␀␀␀OpenTopoMap␀opentopomap␀Tab5OS/0.8.10 (M5Stack Tab5 map viewer)␀https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search␀␀importRate␀␀remember␀␀␀␀tile.openstreetmap.org␀␀tile.opentopomap.org␀␀␀␀tache cartes␀␀␀␀tab5_map_net␀␀␀␀{z}␀{x}␀{y}␀lon␀lat␀home_zoom␀␀␀home_lon␀␀␀␀home_lat␀␀␀␀homeView␀␀␀␀dossier cache␀␀␀.part␀␀␀.t5map␀␀[MAP] paquet hors ligne ignorÃ© : %s
